  "question": "A dot oscillates in a straight line between $A$ and $B$, the edges of a screen $120$ cm wide. Its displacement from $O$, the centre of $AB$, is $x = a\\sin nt$ cm, $t$ s after passing $O$. One oscillation takes $6$ s. (a) Why is $a = 60$? Show that $n = \\frac{1}{3}\\pi$. (b) Find the velocity; deduce the maximum speed. (c) Find the magnitude of the acceleration at $A$.",
